{
  "apiVersion": 1,
  "type": "docs.detail.section",
  "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
  "data": {
    "id": "icon-registry",
    "title": "Built themes with an icon registry",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "`theme build` emits an icon import when it detects a named import used by the theme's `icons:` field. It does not compile that registry module. Move the registry to a separate module and use a named import."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "lang": "bash",
        "code": "# Emit the built theme\nastryx theme build ./src/themes/ocean.ts -o dist/theme.css --icons-specifier ./icons.mjs\n\n# Compile the icon registry alongside it\nesbuild src/themes/icons.tsx --bundle --format=esm --outfile=dist/icons.mjs \\\n  --external:react --external:lucide-react --jsx=automatic",
        "label": "Compiling the icon registry sidecar"
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "In the example above, the generated theme imports `./icons.mjs` from `dist`. If the second command is skipped, `theme build` can still succeed, but loading or bundling the generated module fails because `dist/icons.mjs` is missing. `--icons-specifier` changes the emitted import; it does not create or verify the target file. Match the specifier to a module that resolves from the generated JS file."
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "Without `--icons-specifier`, the detected source import specifier is emitted unchanged. In the default flow without `--out`, a bundler can resolve an extensionless `./icons` to the neighboring `icons.tsx` source, but Node ESM does not perform that lookup and reports `ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND`. Moving the output with `--out` also changes where relative imports resolve from."
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "Keep `react` and the icon library external so the registry does not bundle its own copies of those dependencies."
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "A registry entry can be a function of `{size, variant}`. The built theme keeps the function, so `Icon` asks it for the size and variant it renders, as the runtime theme does, including for entries inherited from a built or package theme. The built theme's `icons` field and the registry its module re-exports are React nodes, with each function read at size `md`. A function written in the theme file itself cannot be carried, so the build fails; move it into the registry module."
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "A theme that lists `iconVariants` also writes an `IconVariantMap` augmentation into `<theme>.variants.d.ts`, so `Icon`'s `variant` accepts those names wherever the theme's types load. Its declaration carries the list too, so a theme that extends the built theme types `variant` in its icon entries by that list."
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "A built theme keeps its `componentIcons`. Names, `null` values, and static requests are written into the module. A slot function stays a function: the module imports it from the module the theme source imports it from, so component slots resolve the same for the built theme as for the runtime theme. The built theme's `componentIcons` field leaves out slot functions, as the runtime theme's does. A slot function defined in the theme file fails the build: move it to its own module and import it. In `--family` output, a member supplies its own slot functions through a named import of its whole `componentIcons` map. The module keeps each slot import as the theme source spells it, and `--icons-specifier` does not change it, so with `--out` in another directory, make a module answer to that specifier from the output directory, as for the icon registry."
      }
    ],
    "links": {
      "up": "astryx docs author-a-theme --index",
      "previous": "astryx docs author-a-theme building-themes-for-production",
      "next": "astryx docs author-a-theme building-a-theme-family"
    }
  },
